#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:1
msgid "Doctest Formatting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:3
msgid ""
"While _Black_ makes some decisions about styling for docstrings, it does not "
"make any assumptions about the contents of documentation. Thus, executable "
"Python code inside docstrings or documentation files (e.g. doctests), will "
"not be formatted by _Black_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:7
msgid ""
"Listed below are tools that apply _Black_ formatting to code inside "
"docstrings and documentation files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:10
msgid ""
"Note: There are some observed inconsistencies between the below packages. "
"Because of this, we hesitate to make any recommendations. Any installed "
"packages are installed at your own risk. We also encourage anyone to "
"contribute documentation for additional packages that apply _Black_ "
"formatting to doctests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:15
msgid "blacken-docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:17
msgid ""
"[`blacken-docs`](https://github.com/adamchainz/blacken-docs) is primarily "
"used to apply _Black_ formatting to code in documentation files (e.g. "
"`.rst`, `.md`, `.tex`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:20
msgid ""
"`blacken-docs` supports Python code blocks and Pycon doctests in Markdown, "
"reStructuredText, and LaTeX files, as well as Python docstrings containing "
"Markdown code blocks and Pycon doctests. It will not format any file "
"contents that _Black_ will already format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:25
msgid ""
"```python\n"
"print(\"Hello world!\")\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```pycon\n"
">>> print(\"Hello world!\")\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:35
msgid ""
".. code-block:: python\n"
"    print(\"Hello world!\")\n"
"\n"
".. code-block:: pycon\n"
"    >>> print(\"Hello world!\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:43
msgid ""
"\\begin{pycode}\n"
"print(\"hello world\")\n"
"\\end{pycode}\n"
"\n"
"\\begin{minted}{pycon}\n"
">>> print(\"hello world\")\n"
"\\end{minted}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:53
msgid ""
"\"\"\"\n"
"```python\n"
"print(\"Hello world!\")\n"
"```\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"\n"
"def add_one(n: int) -> int:\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"    Examples\n"
"    --------\n"
"    ```pycon\n"
"    >>> add_one(1) == 2\n"
"    ```\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"    return n + 1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:71
msgid "blackdoc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:73
msgid ""
"[`blackdoc`](https://blackdoc.readthedocs.io/en/stable) is primarily used to "
"apply _Black_ formatting to doctests in Python files. It will not format any "
"file contents that _Black_ will already format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:77
msgid "`blackdoc` supports the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:79
msgid "Doctests in Python files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:81
msgid ""
"def add_one(n: int) -> int:\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"    Examples\n"
"    --------\n"
"    >>> add_one(1) == 2\n"
"    \"\"\"\n"
"    return n + 1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:91
msgid "Python code blocks and doctests in reStructuredText files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../integrations/doctest_formatting.md:93
msgid ""
".. code-block:: python\n"
"   print(\"Hello world!\")\n"
"\n"
">>> print(\"Hello world!\")\n"
msgstr ""
